cff-version: 1.2.0

message: >-
  If you use this software or its results in academic work,
  please cite this repository.

title: >-
  Sistema explicable de detección preventiva de indicadores de riesgo
  en salud mental adulta mediante aprendizaje automático multisalida
  y agentes de inteligencia artificial generativa a partir del dataset
  NSDUH 2024 / Explainable system for preventive detection of risk
  indicators in adult mental health using multi-output machine learning
  and generative AI agents based on the NSDUH 2024 dataset

type: software

authors:
  - family-names: "Ayllón Motto"
    given-names: "Carlos"

version: "1.0.0"

repository-code: "https://github.com/ayllonmotto/TFM_NSDUH_CAM"

license: MIT

abstract: >-
  This project presents an explainable academic prototype for the preventive
  detection of four indicators related to adult mental health using the
  National Survey on Drug Use and Health (NSDUH) 2024. The final system
  combines a hybrid Machine Learning and Deep Learning predictive solution,
  SHAP-based explainability, and a generative AI agent layer integrating
  structured validation, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), LangGraph,
  Mistral, and guardrails. The repository includes the five main project
  notebooks, experimental results, final inference files, reproducibility
  documentation, productization components, and a local demonstration
  dashboard. The system is intended exclusively for academic and preventive
  research purposes and does not constitute a clinical diagnostic tool.

keywords:
  - machine learning
  - deep learning
  - multi-output classification
  - explainable artificial intelligence
  - XAI
  - SHAP
  - generative artificial intelligence
  - generative AI
  - RAG
  - LangGraph
  - Mistral
  - mental health
  - preventive detection
  - NSDUH
  - reproducible research
